    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The total volume of two identical cube-shaped water tanks is $100\\text{ m}^3$. Calculate the side length of one tank. Round your answer to 2 d.p.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sqrt[3]{50}\\text{ m}\\approx3.68\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "Let the side length of each tank be $x$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^3&=100\\\\x^3&=50\\\\x&=\\sqrt[3]{50}\\\\x&\\approx3.68\\end{align*}$$\nThe side length is approximately $3.68\\text{ m}$.",
